# Scripts that CANNOT be launched by launchd (#1867).
#
# One REPO-RELATIVE path per line. `#` starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
# scripts/install-launchd.sh REFUSES (hard, non-zero, nothing installed) any
# template whose ProgramArguments name one of these scripts, and reports the
# documented launch path instead.
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A gate that can never open is not a gate, and the installer used to install one while reporting
# success. Measured 2026-10-16 on the Mac the heartbeat runs on:
#
#     launchd-spawned instance:  1,695 x "lane-status: DEGRADED"
#                                  210 x "lane-actions: REFUSING a DEGRADED snapshot"
#                                    0 x nudges delivered
#
# with the cmux control socket answering every tick:
#
#     cmux send -> rc=1 :: Access denied - only processes started inside cmux can connect
#
# `socketControlMode` is `cmuxOnly`, so the socket gates on the LAUNCH-CHAIN ATTRIBUTION macOS keeps
# for the process tree — not on parentage. A process that STARTED inside a cmux terminal keeps
# access after it is orphaned (`real_ppid=1`, verified 3/3), and so do its children. A launchd job
# never had it, so every job listed here is BLIND under launchd: it runs, it logs, it does nothing,
# and the log reads as activity. That is the false PASS this manifest exists to make impossible.
#
# ⛔ THE FIX IS THE LAUNCH PATH, NOT THE SOCKET. Relaxing `automation.socketControlMode` from
# `cmuxOnly` to `automation` widens "only processes started inside cmux" to "any process by this
# user" for the whole machine. That is an OWNER DECISION, argued on its own issue — never smuggled
# in through a bug fix.
#
# ── THE DOCUMENTED PATH ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Instead of a timer, the correct portable shape is a DETACHED LAUNCHED-ONCE LOOP, started from any
# cmux-attributed shell:
#
#     bash scripts/heartbeat-launch.sh start        # refuses under launchd, names the path
#     bash scripts/heartbeat-launch.sh status
#     bash scripts/heartbeat-launch.sh check        # behaviour probe: 0 OK / 1 DRIFT / 2 UNKNOWN
#
# The full contract, and the macOS/Linux divergence, is docs/ops/heartbeat-launch-path.md.
#
# ⛔ PARITY NOTE — this file governs the LAUNCHD renderer only. On a Linux cell there is no cmux
# desktop app and therefore no `cmuxOnly` socket, so the same loop is LEGITIMATE there. It is NOT
# delivered there by anything: `scripts/fleet-schedule.py` (the #1864 runtime, CLOSED) schedules exactly these
# `templates/launchd/*.plist` declarations, and THIS FILE is what forbids a template from naming the
# loop — so on a cell the loop is hand-started or not running at all, and delivering it is **#4075**
# (which owns that divergence; #1864 was closed for the SCHEDULER's portability and cannot carry a
# launched-once loop). Stated this way because this comment used to claim fleet-schedule delivered it,
# contradicting docs/ops/heartbeat-launch-path.md and the launcher's own `--help` header (which were
# corrected first — round 9 — and this manifest was missed; round 19 found the same class again, this
# time the OWNER being a closed issue, so grep this file and the doc together for the issue number).
#
# ── MATCHING RULE (stated so a reader can predict the refusal) ──────────────────────────────────
# A ProgramArguments entry matches when its path ends with `/<entry>`. Repo-relative suffix, not
# absolute prefix: the farmed deployment copy (`$HOME/.pi/agent/scripts/<name>`) and a worktree copy
# must both refuse, because the gate is a property of the SCRIPT, not of where it is checked out.
# ⛔ DECLARED RESIDUAL (agent-infra#3826): a *renamed copy or symlink* of a gated script under another
# basename is NOT matched — there is no path resolution here, by design, because resolving would have
# to reproduce the operator's whole filesystem to be complete. MEASURED: a symlink
# `/tmp/…/loop-alias.sh -> <repo>/scripts/heartbeat-loop.sh`, named by a template, installs rc=0.
# The gate catches the natural shapes — the repo path, the farmed path, a `Program`-only plist, and
# `[/bin/bash, …/scripts/heartbeat-loop.sh]` — and a wrapper under a new name is a deliberate evasion,
# not the accident this exists to stop. Closing it needs dev+inode comparison of the resolved target,
# which is the follow-up, not a silent gap: it is stated here so a reader can predict it.
scripts/heartbeat-loop.sh
